<title>RUSSIA: Russia's Tatneft gets $90 mln credit.</title>
<headline>Russia's Tatneft gets $90 mln credit.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian oil company AO Tatneft received a $90 million syndicated credit from a number of Western banks led by Chase Manhattan, Tatneft's financial adviser Bank Zenit said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The funds will be used, in part, to finance investment projects in the republic of Tatarstan, where Tatneft is located, Bank Zenit said in a statement.</p>
<p>Other banks in the syndicate include Banque Worms, Natexis Banque and CS First Boston, the statement said.</p>
